 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added (Sentinel-1 download from 2014 in the fine-tuning notebook, 2026-11-09)
+- `pipeline/gee_s1.py` (helper): Earth Engine catalog of Sentinel-1 IW VV+VH acquisitions over the AMA since 2014-10-03 (first scene in `COPERNICUS/S1_GRD`), with the share of the AOI each one covers; `pick_scene` chooses one acquisition date around a target date (full AOI cover, single pass / relative orbit, closest in time); `export_scene` exports it to Drive with the same parameters as `02a` (10 m, EPSG:32721, VV+VH dB). The picking logic is tested in `tests/test_gee_s1.py`; the Earth Engine calls are mock-tested only, never run live.
+- `notebooks/AMA_finetune_labels_colab.ipynb`, new step 4: availability table per year and orbit, scene choice per event with the rejected candidates shown, download to Drive, `escenas_elegidas.json` for traceability, and an optional series (`SERIE_PASO_MESES`) of one scene every N months from 2014 on a fixed orbit. `EVENTS` entries take only a date now (`scene=` still allowed for scenes already at hand). Why: events before 2014-10 have no Sentinel-1 in GEE, and mixing orbits or dates in one mosaic changes the incidence angle and the backscatter the network sees.
+- Notebook steps after the old step 3 are renumbered (+1).
+
 ### Added (local fine-tuning, 2026-11-04)
 - `pipeline/01c_prepare_ama_chips.py` (+ `make ama-chips`): cuts 512 px chips from an AMA Sentinel-1 scene (mixed water/land chips + hard negatives) and pre-labels them with the stage-1 network into `labels.gpkg` (layers `chips`, `water`), so labels are made by correcting polygons in QGIS instead of drawing them. Optional `ignore.gpkg` marks doubtful areas (label 255).
 - `pipeline/01d_finetune_ama.py` (+ `make finetune`): rasterises the edited polygons and fine-tunes the network with a small LR, mixing Sen1Floods11 batches (`--replay-weight`) against forgetting; validates on held-out AMA events (`--val-events`); saves `unet_ama_best.keras` only if it beats the starting model on the AMA validation chips; reports IoU before/after on AMA and on Sen1Floods11 validation. Why: Sen1Floods11 has no Paraguay, so the stage-2 inventory error in the AMA is unmeasured; this both measures it (held-out AMA chips) and reduces it. `tests/test_ama_finetune.py`.
